WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:04.240
Everyone knows there's nothing&nbsp;
quite like a good tearjerker ending,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:04.240 --> 00:00:10.400
but did you know Twin Peaks had not one but two?&nbsp;
This list includes a few you might not expect.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:10.400 --> 00:00:13.080
Be warned, though: here there be spoilers...

00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:19.200
The second and final season of Fleabag proudly&nbsp;
announces in its first episode that it's going&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:19.200 --> 00:00:24.400
to be "a love story." By the end of the season,&nbsp;
though, you realize that it's not necessarily a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.400 --> 00:00:29.520
love story with a happy ending. The season's&nbsp;
thrust involves the titular character falling&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:29.520 --> 00:00:34.720
for a priest, who ultimately decides to&nbsp;
remain devoted to God. In the final scene,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:40.000
he visits her at a bus stop, and she tells him&nbsp;
that she loves him. His reply is devastating:

00:00:40.821 --> 00:00:41.461
"It'll pass."

00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:45.680
So in the end, Fleabag doesn't get to be with him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:51.440
even though he admits he loves her as well. It's&nbsp;
a terribly sad ending, even when you realize, by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:57.760
the end, that Fleabag will probably be okay. In a&nbsp;
gesture that suggests the finality of the ending,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.160
she walks away from the camera that's been&nbsp;
following her this entire time. She no longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.480
needs to share her life with the audience,&nbsp;
and the audience too needs to be okay with it.

00:01:07.280 --> 00:01:11.680
The final moments of Six Feet Under were&nbsp;
almost certainly designed in a lab to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:17.280
completely devastate everyone who loves the&nbsp;
show. As Claire, the baby of the Fisher family,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.000
drives away from the life she's known,&nbsp;
the show transitions to a montage in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:26.000
which every single one of the show's&nbsp;
recurring characters meet their maker.

00:01:26.000 --> 00:01:31.520
It's a perfect summation of death's beauty and&nbsp;
inevitability. The show suggests that each of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:31.520 --> 00:01:37.200
its main characters go on to lead meaningful&nbsp;
lives, and then, at some point, pass away — as&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:42.400
all people must. It doesn't treat death as&nbsp;
a cudgel, or as something that only exists&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:47.520
to get an emotional reaction out of viewers.&nbsp;
Instead, Six Feet Under shows death as what it is:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.520 --> 00:01:52.880
A natural part of being alive. Everything is&nbsp;
temporary, and in the final moments of the series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:56.840
the show provides a gut-wrenching&nbsp;
reminder to hold on to what you've got.

00:01:57.840 --> 00:02:02.880
Although it's only five episodes long,&nbsp;
Chernobyl nevertheless leaves a huge impact&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:08.400
on its audience. The series tells the story of&nbsp;
the Chernobyl disaster, with particular focus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:14.320
on the bureaucracy that proved so ineffectual in&nbsp;
dealing with the crisis. In its final episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:14.320 --> 00:02:18.993
the show depicts the USSR's half-hearted&nbsp;
effort to hold people accountable for this.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:19.680 --> 00:02:25.520
Ultimately, a few low-level men inside the&nbsp;
facility are held responsible, while the entire&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:25.520 --> 00:02:31.280
system that they existed within is ignored. The&nbsp;
lies that were told about the Chernobyl facility,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:36.240
and the conditions that led the facility&nbsp;
to be unsafe, are not reckoned with at all.

00:02:36.240 --> 00:02:42.400
In the end, Valery Legasov, the crusader who&nbsp;
wanted to change how the USSR handles its nuclear&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:42.400 --> 00:02:47.920
facilities, is revealed to have taken his own&nbsp;
life. He knows that the change he longs for will&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:47.920 --> 00:02:53.600
not come, that people are much happier living with&nbsp;
the lie. And that is a truth he cannot live with.

00:02:55.200 --> 00:03:00.320
Although each series of Blackadder is set in&nbsp;
a different era in history, the show's overall&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:06.560
tone always remains relatively constant. The&nbsp;
show's final season, Blackadder Goes Forth,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:06.560 --> 00:03:11.680
places the show's antihero and his supporting&nbsp;
cast in the trenches of World War I.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:15.280
Because it's a comedy, you might be&nbsp;
tempted to assume that Blackadder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.280 --> 00:03:19.200
is going to trivialize the grim&nbsp;
nature of the war it's depicting.

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:24.160
But the show takes the opposite approach. In&nbsp;
its final episode, Blackadder and the rest&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:24.160 --> 00:03:28.720
of the show's characters realize that they&nbsp;
are about to be sent on a suicide mission.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.720 --> 00:03:33.760
They spend much of the episode attempting&nbsp;
to escape from their fate, but to no avail.

00:03:33.760 --> 00:03:34.605
"Good luck, everyone."

00:03:36.800 --> 00:03:42.000
In the show's final moments, they charge out of&nbsp;
their trench and are presumably mowed down in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:42.000 --> 00:03:48.000
a hail of gunfire. Few shows are bold enough to&nbsp;
kill off their entire main cast in their finale,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:50.535
but that's precisely what Blackadder does.

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:55.200
The finale was widely acclaimed after&nbsp;
it aired, not just for its bravery,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:00.000
but also for the ruthlessness with which&nbsp;
it is able to depict the horrors of war.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:00.480 --> 00:04:07.280
During World War I, countless soldiers were sent&nbsp;
to die totally meaningless deaths — and Blackadder&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.280 --> 00:04:10.890
is one of the few shows willing&nbsp;
to depict that reality in full.

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:16.800
The final moments of Twin Peaks are anything&nbsp;
but uplifting. Disregarding The Return,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.800 --> 00:04:21.200
which functions more as a sequel than as&nbsp;
a continuation of the original series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:21.200 --> 00:04:27.120
Twin Peaks' season two finale leaves things in&nbsp;
a pretty dire state for its heroes. Initially,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:27.120 --> 00:04:31.440
you're led to believe that Dale Cooper&nbsp;
has managed to enter the Black Lodge,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.440 --> 00:04:36.000
rescue Annie Blackburn, and return&nbsp;
to the town of Twin Peaks unharmed.

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.560
In the show's final moments, however, it&nbsp;
becomes clear that Dale Cooper is no longer&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.560 --> 00:04:47.360
the stand-up FBI agent he was at the beginning of&nbsp;
the series. Instead, he's been corrupted by Bob,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:52.400
the evil presence at the heart of the town who&nbsp;
is responsible for the death of Laura Palmer.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.400 --> 00:04:57.840
In the final moments of its original run, Twin&nbsp;
Peaks pulls the rug out from under its audience,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:57.840 --> 00:05:03.600
revealing that the show's stalwart hero is&nbsp;
gone, having been replaced by a vision of pure,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:03.600 --> 00:05:08.320
unbridled evil. And although Coop&nbsp;
certainly wouldn't be gone forever,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:11.120
it's not like The Return gave him&nbsp;
much of a happy ending, either...

00:05:12.080 --> 00:05:15.760
Veep's ending isn't sad in the&nbsp;
sense that it might make you cry.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:15.760 --> 00:05:21.600
Rather, the show devotes its final episode to&nbsp;
the emptiness of politics. As Selina attempts&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:21.600 --> 00:05:27.440
to win her party's nomination for president, she&nbsp;
reveals that she's willing to sacrifice everyone&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:27.440 --> 00:05:32.560
and everything she's supposed to care about in&nbsp;
order to get it. She trades away her principles&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:32.560 --> 00:05:37.680
to earn support from other wings of her party,&nbsp;
and blames Gary, the person who has been at her&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:37.680 --> 00:05:43.280
side throughout the entirety of the show, for&nbsp;
an FBI investigation into her charity fund.

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:48.240
Selina betrays everyone — and as a&nbsp;
result, she gets exactly what she wants.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:51.600
Ultimately, though, viewers know&nbsp;
that her victory is a hollow one,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:51.600 --> 00:05:56.640
because it comes at the cost of every character&nbsp;
they've grown to love. From its first episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:56.640 --> 00:06:01.680
Veep presents a world in which what you achieve&nbsp;
as an influential politician matters far&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:01.680 --> 00:06:07.840
less than how much power you accumulate. In its&nbsp;
finale, Veep doubles down on that brutal theme&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:07.840 --> 00:06:13.160
and digs into the dark heart of what makes&nbsp;
the American political system so absurd.

00:06:14.160 --> 00:06:20.000
The ending of Parenthood is dark in a uniquely&nbsp;
simple way: It focuses on the death of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:20.000 --> 00:06:26.400
Braverman family's patriarch, Zeek. The show's&nbsp;
final moments take place after Zeek's death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:26.400 --> 00:06:30.720
as we see the rest of the Bravermans&nbsp;
assemble to play baseball in his honor.

00:06:30.720 --> 00:06:36.320
It's a beautiful, moving tribute that acts as a&nbsp;
reminder of the legacy that Zeek has left behind.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.320 --> 00:06:41.600
He created the family at the center of the series,&nbsp;
and in its final moments, the show chooses to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:41.600 --> 00:06:47.600
spotlight that. Zeek's death is a sad event, but&nbsp;
Parenthood reminds its audience that feeling sad&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:47.600 --> 00:06:52.400
is just one part of the human experience.&nbsp;
Losing Zeek feels like losing a member of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:52.400 --> 00:06:57.600
your family should: It breaks your heart, but it&nbsp;
also gives you a chance to remember all the great&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:57.600 --> 00:07:03.280
things the person did while they were alive. It's&nbsp;
bittersweet, contemplative, and totally honest.

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:08.320
How do you end a show when your principal&nbsp;
characters have been dead the whole time?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:08.320 --> 00:07:13.520
As it turns out, the answer is to kill them&nbsp;
again. In the final episode of The Good Place,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.520 --> 00:07:18.640
all four core members of the show's human cast&nbsp;
have all finally arrived in the Good Place.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:23.280
Once there, they're able to fulfill&nbsp;
every desire they've ever had.

00:07:23.280 --> 00:07:28.240
Eventually, though, they realize that they're&nbsp;
ready to move on, and essentially phase out of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.240 --> 00:07:34.800
existence itself. It's a concept that's almost&nbsp;
too heady for TV, but Chidi, ever the professor,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:34.800 --> 00:07:39.680
explains it well. Life in The Good Place is&nbsp;
like a wave: Once you crash on the shore,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.680 --> 00:07:44.000
you disappear, but the water you&nbsp;
leave behind is still very much there.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:50.720
"The wave was just a different way for&nbsp;
the water to be for a little while."

00:07:51.920 --> 00:07:56.160
The Good Place's finale is about learning&nbsp;
to accept the end of your own existence.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.800 --> 00:08:01.920
Specifically, it's about willingly relinquishing&nbsp;
your identity and becoming a positive force in the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:01.920 --> 00:08:07.200
universe. Death isn't the end for the show's&nbsp;
main characters, but in the final episode,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:07.200 --> 00:08:11.840
they all blink out of existence for good — in&nbsp;
a way that goes far beyond the mere stopping&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:11.840 --> 00:08:17.120
point that is physical death. The show makes clear&nbsp;
that they've all accepted this choice, of course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:20.200
but that doesn't mean it's&nbsp;
not utterly heartbreaking.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.200
After 11 seasons on the air, no one&nbsp;
expected M*A*S*H to do anything all&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:30.720
that daring in its final episode. The series&nbsp;
finale chronicles the end of the Korean War,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:30.720 --> 00:08:35.600
and the party that the members of the camp throw&nbsp;
before they say their tear-filled goodbyes to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:40.960
one another. Before those farewells happen,&nbsp;
though, the show offers up a meaty plot about&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:40.960 --> 00:08:45.600
the weight of the conflict, and what it's done&nbsp;
to Hawkeye Pierce, the show's main character.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:51.680
In this episode, Hawkeye revisits a traumatic&nbsp;
incident that occured as his unit was returning&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:51.680 --> 00:08:57.040
from a beach outing. Their bus eventually picked&nbsp;
up a number of refugees, but was forced to pull&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:57.040 --> 00:09:02.480
off the road in order to avoid being spotted.&nbsp;
Hawkeye specifically recalls telling a woman&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:02.480 --> 00:09:07.200
to quiet her chicken, and the woman killing&nbsp;
the chicken to keep it from making noise.

00:09:07.200 --> 00:09:09.838
"Everybody's life was in danger&nbsp;
because of that damn chicken."

00:09:10.640 --> 00:09:15.360
Later on in the episode, it's revealed&nbsp;
that Hawkeye has repressed the real memory:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:15.360 --> 00:09:21.120
It wasn't a chicken she was trying to keep silent,&nbsp;
but her own baby. The woman smothered her child&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:26.720
in order to survive, and Hawkeye can't cope&nbsp;
with the reality of that memory. It's a dark,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:26.720 --> 00:09:32.240
dark turn for the final episode of the show, but&nbsp;
one that feels necessary. Even though M*A*S*H&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:32.240 --> 00:09:37.480
is ostensibly a comedy, it never shies away&nbsp;
from depicting the brutal realities of war.

00:09:38.480 --> 00:09:43.280
The series finale of Merlin plays out like&nbsp;
a brutal tragedy. From the very beginning,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:43.280 --> 00:09:48.080
the show is centered around the friendship&nbsp;
between Arthur and Merlin. As Arthur ascends&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.080 --> 00:09:52.400
the throne and heads off to adventure with&nbsp;
the rest of the knights of the round table,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:56.800
the show’s primary interest doesn't&nbsp;
change. In the final episode, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:56.800 --> 00:10:01.280
Arthur is struck down, and Merlin is&nbsp;
unable to revive him. He's told that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:01.280 --> 00:10:05.840
Arthur will rise again, but neither Merlin&nbsp;
nor the audience gets to see that happen.

00:10:06.480 --> 00:10:11.840
Instead, the episode follows Merlin as he spends&nbsp;
millennia waiting for his friend to come again.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:17.680
He's an ageless, eternal being, doomed to be&nbsp;
traumatized by a past that he has no power to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:17.680 --> 00:10:22.160
change. While the rest of the characters&nbsp;
in Merlin get to live complete arcs,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:22.160 --> 00:10:28.080
the show's central figure must remain in stasis.&nbsp;
The life he leads now is one a life of waiting.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:28.080 --> 00:10:33.680
He's lost his best friend, and now, all he can do&nbsp;
is pray that he'll get to see him again… someday.

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:40.160
The ending of How I Met Your Mother was hugely&nbsp;
anticipated by the show's fans. That excitement&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:40.160 --> 00:10:45.120
stemmed in part from the show's premise, which&nbsp;
suggests that eventually, Ted will get to the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:45.120 --> 00:10:50.480
part of the story that involves his wife. The&nbsp;
finale does indeed reveal their first meeting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:54.320
before offering an abbreviated look at&nbsp;
what his life with his kids' mother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:54.320 --> 00:11:00.160
played by Cristin Milioti, went on to be like.&nbsp;
It's just as sweet and romantic as fans hoped for.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:06.560
The episode ultimately reveals, however, that&nbsp;
the mother died in 2024. She and Ted built a life&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:06.560 --> 00:11:12.400
together, but it wasn't one meant to last forever.&nbsp;
Although Milioti only plays a prominent role in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:12.400 --> 00:11:18.000
the final arc of the show's run, she made such an&nbsp;
enormous impression on audiences that her death&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:18.000 --> 00:11:24.000
proved to be a deeply sad and divisive event. The&nbsp;
entire show builds up to the mother's arrival,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:29.440
and when audiences finally meet her, she doesn't&nbsp;
disappoint — but the show's decisions might.

00:11:29.440 --> 00:11:34.080
How I Met Your Mother's final episode became&nbsp;
further controversial for suggesting that,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:34.080 --> 00:11:39.120
after the mother's death, Ted ultimately&nbsp;
falls back in love with Robin. To many,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.120 --> 00:11:43.520
this choice rings hollow, in part because of all&nbsp;
the hype that had been built around the mother.

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:49.520
If you present a simple and factual account&nbsp;
of what happens at the end of The Americans,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:49.520 --> 00:11:54.640
it might not seem all that devastating. Philip&nbsp;
and Elizabeth, the Russian spies at the center&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:54.640 --> 00:12:00.880
of the show, manage to safely return to the USSR&nbsp;
after spending years living as Americans. In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:00.880 --> 00:12:05.518
order to make their escape, though, they have to&nbsp;
give up the entire life they've built in the US.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.160 --> 00:12:10.080
Their daughter, who was supposed to&nbsp;
join them on their journey to the USSR,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:10.080 --> 00:12:14.560
decides to stay behind, and it's unclear&nbsp;
whether they'll ever see her again.

00:12:14.560 --> 00:12:20.560
When you dig into the human emotion at the core of&nbsp;
this finale, its true tragedy is revealed. Philip&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:25.200
has to tell his best friend that he's been lying&nbsp;
to him for years, and entrust him with looking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:30.400
after the son they're leaving behind. What's&nbsp;
more, the society they're returning to is on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:30.400 --> 00:12:36.000
the brink of collapse. All of the crimes and the&nbsp;
lies that the two of them have been caught up in,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:40.240
all for the sake of their homeland, will have&nbsp;
been for nothing. They built their lives in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:40.240 --> 00:12:45.360
the US and were forced to abandon those lives&nbsp;
for a country they haven't lived in for years.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:45.360 --> 00:12:50.240
And then, at the end of it all, that failing&nbsp;
country makes it perfectly clear that it doesn't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:50.240 --> 00:12:55.040
actually care about them. It's a crushing&nbsp;
final blow for the show's protagonists.

00:12:56.160 --> 00:13:01.040
The final episode of The Leftovers has a happy&nbsp;
ending, but it's one that comes after an enormous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:06.640
amount of trauma. The finale is set more than&nbsp;
a decade in the future, as Nora lives a quiet,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:06.640 --> 00:13:12.960
remote life in Australia. That life faces a huge&nbsp;
disruption when Kevin, her former boyfriend and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:12.960 --> 00:13:18.080
the love of her life, shows up out of the blue.&nbsp;
The entire episode is built on the weight of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:18.080 --> 00:13:22.960
the history between these two characters, and&nbsp;
that history is more than a little grueling.

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:27.760
When they finally reconcile, it's a moment&nbsp;
of enormous relief, and a reminder of how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:27.760 --> 00:13:32.720
far they've both come. The Leftovers is set&nbsp;
in a world in which two percent of the world's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:32.720 --> 00:13:38.080
population has inexplicably vanished, and&nbsp;
the show's finale chooses not to provide any&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:38.080 --> 00:13:43.600
firm answers about this. Instead, it suggests&nbsp;
that what matters is how its characters feel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:47.520
and whether or not they've been able&nbsp;
to overcome their struggles. Indeed,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:47.520 --> 00:13:53.440
Kevin and Nora have certainly struggled before,&nbsp;
but the finale suggests that maybe, just maybe,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:53.440 --> 00:13:57.360
there might be cause for hope. It's an&nbsp;
optimistic ending, but one that serves&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:13:57.360 --> 00:14:01.190
to highlight the deep sadness that the two&nbsp;
of them have shared throughout the series.

00:14:02.347 --> 00:14:07.760
BoJack Horseman's final episode opens with the&nbsp;
titular character being rescued from the pool&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:07.760 --> 00:14:11.680
at his former house. He winds&nbsp;
up in prison for trespassing,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:11.680 --> 00:14:16.400
and finds that the routine his life takes on&nbsp;
in jail helps him in his battle with addiction.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:16.400 --> 00:14:21.840
The finale then leaps forward one year. BoJack&nbsp;
is released for Princess Carolyn's wedding,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:26.320
where he sees all of his old friends again.&nbsp;
But it becomes increasingly clear that these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:26.320 --> 00:14:30.640
friendships, which have been the core&nbsp;
of the series, may not last forever.

00:14:30.640 --> 00:14:34.560
BoJack is a better person than he was&nbsp;
when the show started, but he's done&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:39.600
irreparable harm to the people he's supposed&nbsp;
to care about most. They still love Bojack,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:39.600 --> 00:14:43.120
but they know that if they're looking&nbsp;
to build healthy lives for themselves,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:43.120 --> 00:14:48.000
they might have to leave him behind. As&nbsp;
Diane, BoJack's closest confidant, tells him:

00:14:48.640 --> 00:14:52.560
"I think there are people that help you&nbsp;
become the person who you end up being,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:14:52.560 --> 00:14:57.840
and you can be grateful for them, even if they&nbsp;
were never meant to be in your life forever."

00:14:58.480 --> 00:15:03.520
The finale of BoJack Horseman is about knowing&nbsp;
when relationships have run their course,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:03.520 --> 00:15:06.800
and allowing people to leave your&nbsp;
life, even if it hurts in the moment.

00:15:07.920 --> 00:15:12.000
When They See Us has an ending that&nbsp;
could actually be described as happy.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:12.480 --> 00:15:17.680
The Central Park Five, who have spent years in&nbsp;
prison, are eventually exonerated for the crime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:17.680 --> 00:15:22.640
of sexually assaulting a woman, and the real&nbsp;
criminal is brought to justice. In the end,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:22.640 --> 00:15:27.440
their story is one of triumph, but&nbsp;
that triumph comes at an enormous cost.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:27.440 --> 00:15:31.600
The young kids at the core of the series&nbsp;
have been brutalized by a system that was&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:31.600 --> 00:15:35.920
built to automatically assume the&nbsp;
worst of young Black men like them.

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:40.640
These characters have been traumatized, and&nbsp;
the fact that they are eventually exonerated&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:40.640 --> 00:15:45.360
does not erase what has happened to them.&nbsp;
When They See Us sheds a light on the crime&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:45.360 --> 00:15:50.080
that was perpetrated against these boys,&nbsp;
and what it reveals is devastating. They&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:50.080 --> 00:15:55.440
were totally unable to defend themselves, and so&nbsp;
they were swallowed up by a vicious establishment.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:15:55.440 --> 00:15:58.480
The fact that they're spat out&nbsp;
again is little comfort to anyone.

00:15:59.600 --> 00:16:03.680
A TV show about the AIDS crisis&nbsp;
was never going to be a great time,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:03.680 --> 00:16:08.000
but It's a Sin is still a particularly&nbsp;
horrifying reminder of what the early&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:13.840
days of AIDS were truly like in the U.K. The&nbsp;
show follows a group of young, gay Londoners&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:13.840 --> 00:16:18.800
who are thrilled to be able to live their&nbsp;
lives as who they really are. Slowly, though,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:18.800 --> 00:16:24.800
the unfolding AIDS crisis invades and transforms&nbsp;
those lives, as well as the world around them.

00:16:24.800 --> 00:16:29.360
By the end of the show, several of the main&nbsp;
characters have died, and the show's final&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:29.360 --> 00:16:34.720
moments are rooted in the show's protagonist&nbsp;
succumbing to the virus. He was once vibrant,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:34.720 --> 00:16:40.320
cocky, and full of life, but he dies alone in his&nbsp;
childhood bedroom, cut off from his friends by his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:40.320 --> 00:16:45.680
panicked, homophobic mother. It's a Sin is about&nbsp;
what it meant to be gay during this era, and how&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:45.680 --> 00:16:51.360
AIDS redefined an entire generation of people.&nbsp;
It's also about a few particular young men whose&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:16:51.360 --> 00:16:57.553
lives are cut tragically short. The finale brings&nbsp;
this tragedy into sharp and unforgettable focus.

